{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"systemDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<system-distance>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertical distance from the bottom line of the previous system to the top line of the current system, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenths. Ignored for the first system on a page."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"systemDistance","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSystemLayoutV14systemDistanceSdSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"systemDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdistance"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDistance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLSystemLayout","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a group of staves that are read and played simultaneously. System layout includes left and right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"margins and the vertical distance from the previous system. The system distance is measured from the bottom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line of the previous system to the top line of the current system. It is ignored for the first system on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page. The top system distance is measured from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is ignored for all but the first system on a page."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTenths","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout/systemDistance":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertical distance from the bottom line of the previous system to the top line of the current system, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenths. Ignored for the first system on a page."}],"title":"systemDistance","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDistance","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdistance","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"systemDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}}}